runbooks/README.md:41:For games, `F005` creates a project-scoped `game-design-runbooks/` collection.
runbooks/README.md-42-`GD0001` selects the detailed design work from the game's actual design signals,
runbooks/README.md-43-then allocates `GB` writers. Each GB file writes at most five detailed `G`
runbooks/README.md-44-design tasks; `GC` checkpoints validate them, later `GD` files dispatch further
runbooks/README.md-45-waves, and `GQ` performs the final design audit. Supervisor treats this as a
runbooks/README.md:46:prerequisite collection: it completes G work before F006 can create
runbooks/README.md-47-implementation contracts. G files are not generic RPG tasks—an RPG might plan
runbooks/README.md-48-story, world, characters, bosses, quests, and jobs; football trivia might plan
runbooks/README.md-49-question sourcing, categories, adjudication, scoring, fairness, and editorial
