runbooks/README.md-109-intensity—and proposes relevant and rejected design modules. F002 turns only
runbooks/README.md:110:the selected modules into a game-design bible. F005 then produces a concrete,
runbooks/README.md-111-machine-readable production inventory. This avoids treating a game as a fixed
runbooks/README.md-112-RPG template: an RPG can receive named party, world, boss, quest, and ability
runbooks/README.md-113-cards, while a football-trivia game receives question provenance, categories,
--
